# Rank 1503 / CVE-2021-43821: OpenCast's ingest service accepted a media URL
# from the request and fetched it with the local filesystem in scope
# (CWE-552, CWE-918). Two entry points shared the shape: the REST layer's
# updateMediaPackageID(MediaPackage, URI) and the ingest service's download()
# in IngestServiceImpl both branched on uri.toString().startsWith("http") and
# gave every other scheme -- file:///etc/passwd among them -- to
# uri.toURL().openStream(), so an ingest request could make the server read
# local files (the advisory's fix title: "Ensure local files are not
# addable"). Pool commit 65c46b9d3e is the real fix (COMMIT_OK, GHSA-59g4-
# hpg3-3gcp): the service's else branch became
#   else if (!uri.toString().startsWith("file") || testMode)
#       in = uri.toURL().openStream();
#   else throw new IOException("Refusing to fetch files from the local
# filesystem");
# with testMode a protected flag only tests set. No pool correction.
#
# FIXED by a sink binding. The rule VYQL-RF-001 (taint core.UserControlledData
# -> code.UrlFetch, unless AllowlistValidation) had java bindings for
# openConnection, getForObject and getForEntity, but not for URL.openStream,
# which the JDK documents as "opens a connection to this URL and returns an
# InputStream for reading from that connection" -- a URL fetch with the
# connection step folded in. vyql/bindings/java/murlfetch.vyql emits
# code.UrlFetch at openStream's receiver. Measured on the real module
# (modules/ingest-service-impl/.../ingest/, 7 java files): the vulnerable
# revision goes from 72 findings to 73, adding VYQL-RF-001 at medium
# confidence, source code.HttpInput at IngestRestService.java:936 (the @POST
# addTrack family feeding a private URI overload), sink code.UrlFetch at
# IngestRestService.java:966 (uri.toURL().openStream()), the unless clause
# unsatisfied. Two honest limits, recorded rather than papered over: the
# service's own copy of the fetch sits behind the job queue -- addTrack
# serialises the URI into a service-registry job payload and download() reads
# it back, a boundary taint does not cross -- and the endpoint's copy is
# untouched by this fix commit, so the same finding is present at the fixed
# revision too: the detection is the shape, and on this checkout the shape
# survives the fix. The fix's own control -- an inline
# startsWith("file") refusal -- is not expressible as a neutralising control:
# vyql explain on the patched form reports "no neutralizing control dominates
# the path; none found anywhere on flows", startsWith is bound only as an
# advisory core.InputValidation check for trust boundaries, and a java
# AllowlistValidation binding keyed on a scheme literal would be shaped by
# this incident rather than by the JDK's documentation, so none was shipped.
# The finding on the fixed code is defensible: the patch narrowed the file
# scope (CWE-552), not URL provenance, and a user-directed openStream fetch
# of https://attacker.example remains after it. The spec's reject direction
# therefore pins the boundary the rule actually draws, following the
# rank 232 precedent: a URI that is parsed and branched on but never fetched
# is not a request forgery.
#
# verify_current_expected: fixed-sink-binding

test "rank1503: an ingest url that is fetched with the filesystem in scope"
  lang java
  file modules/ingest-service-impl/src/main/java/org/opencastproject/ingest/endpoint/IngestRestService.java
  expect VYQL-RF-001
  code
  ```
  package org.opencastproject.ingest.endpoint;

  import java.io.InputStream;
  import java.net.URI;
  import jakarta.ws.rs.FormParam;
  import jakarta.ws.rs.POST;
  import jakarta.ws.rs.Path;
  import jakarta.ws.rs.core.Response;

  public class IngestRestService {
    private java.net.http.HttpClient httpClient = java.net.http.HttpClient.newHttpClient();

    @POST
    @Path("addTrack")
    public Response addMediaPackageTrack(@FormParam("url") String url) throws Exception {
      return updateMediaPackageId(new URI(url));
    }

    private Response updateMediaPackageId(URI uri) throws Exception {
      InputStream in;
      if (uri.toString().startsWith("http")) {
        java.net.http.HttpRequest get = java.net.http.HttpRequest.newBuilder(uri).build();
        in = httpClient.send(get, java.net.http.HttpResponse.BodyHandlers.ofInputStream()).body();
      } else {
        in = uri.toURL().openStream();
      }
      in.close();
      return Response.ok().build();
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1503: uri parsing with no fetch is not a request forgery"
  lang java
  file modules/ingest-service-impl/src/main/java/org/opencastproject/ingest/impl/IngestServiceImpl.java
  reject VYQL-RF-001
  code
  ```
  package org.opencastproject.ingest.impl;

  import java.net.URI;
  import jakarta.ws.rs.FormParam;
  import jakarta.ws.rs.POST;

  public class IngestServiceImpl {
    @POST
    public String resolveName(@FormParam("url") String url) throws Exception {
      URI uri = new URI(url);
      if (uri.toString().startsWith("file")) {
        return "refused";
      }
      return uri.getPath();
    }
  }
  ```
